{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7781","id":5214289570,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNsu-og","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7781","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7781.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7781.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7781","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7781/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7781/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7781/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/1a4888f4b4e8228d9a82ef8e4400d656815d89a2","number":7781,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(id): residency & boundaries framework skeleton design (#5683)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nDrafts the **residency & boundaries framework skeleton** design record for #5683 step 1 — the shared vocabulary underneath #2283 (jurisdiction-aware stores), #3397 (jurisdiction-partitioned worlds), and #3398 (residency boundaries for bridge/federation/relays).\n\nNew file: `doc/2026-11-08_design_id5683.md` (522 lines). No implementation code.\n\n## Contents\n\n- **§1** Restates Drew's hard framing requirements (capabilities-never-defaults, basic-frameworks-first, not a GDPR product) so child designs cite rather than re-derive them.\n- **§2** Framework shape: capability catalogue, scope-owns-rule vs subject-is-judged, the one `BoundaryDeclaration` format, four failure behaviours ordered by strength.\n- **§3** Evidence model: assurance levels (self / org-attested / provider-verified), provenance, lifetime, privacy classes (`Exact` / `Derived` / `VerdictOnly`), and a table of what each assurance may drive — including the rule that **no weak signal removes access a subject already has**.\n- **§4** Public IP as evidence: derivation, retention, the known error modes (VPN, CGNAT, corporate egress, mobile, satellite, relay), contradiction handling, explicit X-Forwarded-For trust.\n- **§5** Sanctions boundaries as versioned data: propagation, declared scope of interaction, grandfathering on list changes, exception records and appeal path.\n- **§6** Intranet mode: explicitly enabled network boundary predicates, configurable step-up and degraded-mode outcomes, privacy-aware org escrow/proxying, and separately enabled break-glass. No enforcement behavior is an implicit default.\n- **§7** Composability: only explicitly enabled boundaries and user preferences participate; configured outcomes combine through one shared adapter.\n- **§8** Enforcement at signup/login, world membership/blob access, bridge/federation/relay send and receive, retries, metadata, and capability grants; refused payloads are not persisted.\n- **§9** Explicitly reuses the existing `residency.rs` placement vocabulary/evaluator unchanged for placement only; adds typed predicates, a `SubjectEvidence` envelope, and a shared `FrameworkOutcome` adapter without a parallel residency model.\n- **§10** Three worked examples (sanctions-enabled public server, intranet-mode org server, jurisdiction-pinned world).\n- **§11** Remaining choices are explicit per enabled declaration; no assumed enforcement defaults.\n- **§12** Implementation issues #7782–#7787 are filed and natively linked as sub-issues of #5683.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Baseline `origin/main` at `26018ce4e7`.\n- No prior `5683` framework record exists in `doc/`; no open PR references #5683.\n- All 12 `residency.rs` symbols cited in §9 verified present in the file.\n- Child design #5883 (`doc/2026-11-08T09-15-00Z_design_boundary_audit_appeals.md`) confirmed to *rely on* the parent decisions restated here, not replace this record.\n\nDocs-only change; no test suite applies.\n\nCloses #5683 step 1 (design record). Implementation issues are filed and linked from #5683 in the same pass.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796757250&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7781&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7781&signature=dc87efd6db66fc090edf8bd5d81ad8814ee152b5c6e9f4643328b77bd8c36d80\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7781?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith